[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Zephyr System Requirements
PREFIX: ZEP-SYRS-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: system_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Hardware Architecture Interface
TITLE: Architecture Layer Interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework to communicate with a set of hardware architectural services.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to be able to easily switch my application to a different MCU architecture (x86, ARM Cortex-M/A, RISCV etc.).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-2
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Hardware Architecture Interface
TITLE: Support multiprocessor management
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support symmetric multiprocessing on multiple cores.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to use Zephyr OS on multi core (SMP-)MCUs/MPUs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: C Library
TITLE: Support Subset of Standard C Library
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support a subset of the standard C library.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to have a selection of standard C library implementations e.g. a full extend and a minimal with a smaller footprint or a particular fast executing implementation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-4
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Device Drivers
TITLE: Device Driver Abstraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework for managing device drivers and peripherals.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want my application to be portable between different MCU architectures (ARM Cortex-M/A, Intel x86, RISCV etc.) and MCU vendors (STM, NXP, Intel, etc.) without having to change the MCU peripherals access.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Exception and Error Handling
TITLE: Fatal error and exception handling
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework for error and exception handling.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want errors and exceptions to handled and react according to my applications requirements (e.g. reach/establish the applications safety state).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-6
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: File Systems
TITLE: Common File system operation support
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework for managing file system access.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a posix / c like file system access to store data.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Interrupts
TITLE: Interrupt Management
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework for interrupt and interrupt service routine management.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As the Zephyr RTOS user I want the Kernel to provide abstracted interfaces to
the platform enabling me to implement standard interrupts interrupt service routines
without detailed knowledge of the platform architecture and programming model.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-20
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Interrupts
TITLE: Direct ISR, Platform Specific helpers.
STATEMENT: >>>
Zephyr RTOS shall support development of direct ISRs by providing platform specific
code fragments and factory functions including, minimal header instructions,
minimal footer instructions, low power termination, and ISR construction.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As the Zephyr RTOS user I want the Kernel to provide support for implementing standard low latency
and low power interrupt service routines without detailed knowledge of the platform architecture
and programming model.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-7

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Logging
TITLE: Logging
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework for logging events.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to be able to log application defined events as well as framework exceptions.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Memory Management
TITLE: Memory Management framework
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support a memory management framework.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want memory to be allocated and protected to my application threads preventing mistakenly access to foreign memory as far as the hardware allows.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Power Management
TITLE: Power Management
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to control hardware power states.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to be able to control the power mode of the MCU and its peripherals to take advantage of the hardware features and to be able to implement low power or battery driven long life applications.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Multi core and SMP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: SMP and Multi core
TITLE: Multiple CPU scheduling
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support scheduling of threads on multiple hardware CPUs.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want Zephyr OS to run on MCUs/CPUs with one or more CPU cores.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: SMP and Multi core
TITLE: Scheduling
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to assign a thread to a specific CPU.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user, I want to be able to control which thread will run on which CPU.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Thread Synchronization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-13
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Mutex
TITLE: Mutex
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface for managing communication between threads.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to able to exchange information between threads in a thread-safe manner guaranteeing data consistence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-14
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Semaphore
TITLE: Counting Semaphore
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall implement a semaphore synchronization primitive for coordinating access to shared resources among multiple threads.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Threads

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-15
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Threads
TITLE: Thread support
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall support threads.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user, I want to be able to have support for the kernel objects named threads for processing work.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-16
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Threads
TITLE: Thread management
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework for managing multiple threads of execution.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user, I want to be able to manage the execute of multiple threads with different priorities.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-17
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Threads
TITLE: Thread priority
STATEMENT: >>>
Threads shall have a priority.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user, I want to be able to give my threads different priorities for execution.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-18
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Timers
TITLE: Timers
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework for managing time-based events.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user, I want to start, suspend, resume and stop timers which shall trigger an event on a set expiration time.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-19
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Tracing
TITLE: Tracing
STATEMENT: >>>
Zepyhr shall provide a framework mechanism for tracing low level system operations  (NOTE: system calls, interrupts, kernel calls, thread, synchronization, etc.).
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user, I want to be able to trace different OS operations.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Condition Variables

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-21
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Non-Functional
COMPONENT: Condition Variables
TITLE: Condition Variables
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework to synchronize threads based on a condition variable.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Queues

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-22
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Queues
TITLE: Queues data passing
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall implement a queue which can be used to pass data between threads and interrupt service routines.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: LIFOs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-23
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: LIFOs
TITLE: LIFOs data passing
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall implement a LIFOs which can be used to pass data between threads and interrupt service routines.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: FIFOs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-24
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: FIFOs
TITLE: FIFOs data passing
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall implement FIFOs which can be used to pass data between threads and interrupt service routines.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Mailboxes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-25
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Mailboxes
TITLE: Mailboxes
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a framework to pass messages of arbitrary size between threads.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: System Initialization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-26
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: System Initialization
TITLE: Ordered system startup sequence
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall execute a defined sequence of initialization phases during system
startup before transferring control to the application.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a predictable boot sequence with well-defined phases so that
drivers and subsystems are initialized in the correct order.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Kernel Clock and Timing

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-27
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Clock and Timing
TITLE: Kernel timing and sleep services
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide interfaces for reading system time, putting threads to
sleep for specified durations, and specifying timeout values for kernel services.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to delay execution, measure elapsed time and express
timeouts in a portable, hardware-independent way.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Spinlocks

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-28
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Spinlocks
TITLE: Spinlock synchronization primitive
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a spinlock primitive for mutual exclusion between threads
and interrupt service routines, disabling interrupts on the local CPU while held.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want a low-level, IRQ-safe mutual exclusion mechanism for
protecting short critical sections that may be accessed from both thread and ISR context.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Atomic Operations

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-29
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Atomic Operations
TITLE: Atomic variable operations
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a set of operations for reading, writing and modifying
integer variables atomically without requiring explicit locking.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to share integer counters and flags between threads and ISRs
without the overhead of a mutex or spinlock.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Event Objects

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-30
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Event Objects
TITLE: Event object synchronization primitive
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an event object primitive that allows threads to wait on
one or more event bits and allows other threads or ISRs to set or clear those bits.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to signal multiple independent conditions with a single
kernel object and have threads wake up when any or all of the conditions they care about
are satisfied.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Message Queues

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-31
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Fixed-size message queue primitive
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a message queue primitive that allows threads and interrupt
service routines to exchange fixed-size data items through a bounded FIFO buffer with
blocking send and receive semantics.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to pass fixed-size data safely between an ISR and a thread,
or between two threads, without manual buffer management.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Pipes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-32
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Pipes
TITLE: Byte-stream pipe primitive
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a pipe primitive that allows a thread to write a stream of
bytes into a bounded ring buffer and another thread to read from it, with blocking
semantics and timeout support.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to pass an unstructured byte stream between threads using
a producer-consumer model with a configurable internal buffer.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Work Queues

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-33
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Work Queues
TITLE: Work queue execution framework
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a work queue framework that allows deferred execution of
handler functions in a thread context, supporting both immediate and time-delayed
submission.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to defer work from an ISR or a high-priority thread to a
lower-priority thread context without creating a dedicated thread for each deferred task.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Poll

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-34
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Poll
TITLE: Multi-object poll mechanism
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to block a thread on multiple kernel objects
simultaneously, waking when any of the specified objects becomes ready.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user, I want to wait efficiently on multiple event sources (semaphores,
queues, signals) in a single blocking call rather than polling each object individually.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Freedom from Interference

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SYRS-35
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Non-Functional
COMPONENT: Freedom From Interference
TITLE: Freedom from interference between software components
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide mechanisms to prevent unintended interference between
concurrently executing software components, encompassing spatial isolation (memory
partitioning), stack integrity (overflow detection and containment), temporal isolation
(CPU time observability and budget enforcement), and fault containment (localization of
faults to the component that caused them).
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user developing a mixed-criticality or safety-certified system, I want
the kernel to guarantee that a fault, resource overuse, or memory error in one software
component cannot compromise the correct execution of another component, so that I can
demonstrate component independence as required by IEC 61508, ISO 26262, or equivalent
safety standards.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
